 <a id="the-tab-domain"></a>
 ## The Tab domain
 
+An editable tab registers `ctx.sidebarRight.beforeClose(sessionId, tabId, guard)` for its record lifetime. The owner returns `true` to allow removal or `false` to retain the record; a promise defers the whole operation, and an exception or rejection retains it. This covers strip and menu close, floating close, replacement, and every store operation that removes records. Each Session accepts its first pending removal and ignores later removal requests until it settles; navigation and hiding remain available. The executor applies an allowed intent to the latest layout without overwriting changes made while waiting.
+
+The guard receives `{ signal }`; `beforeClose` returns an idempotent registration disposer. Releasing or replacing the owner, removing the record, or unloading the provider cancels outstanding decisions. Keep the registration when a body unmounts for a tab or Session switch. Provider unload aborts all occurrences and waits for its own work to settle without waiting for an owner dialog; an extension owns its draft cleanup and the browser's reload warning. Guards do not persist drafts or block forced unload.
+
 The Tab domain retains navigation, an abort signal, and bound actions per (Session, tab id). A private assembly callback adopts each Session's store and reconciles records on its commits. Only record removal or plugin unload aborts the signal; closing the sidebar and switching Sessions retain records, while undo restores a new occurrence. `useTabInfo()` composes framework-bound store and navigation hooks without manual component subscriptions or render-time record creation. `tab.actions` always target their own Session; `tab.visible` distinguishes bodies from titles, and floating tabs remain visible when the sidebar closes. `adopt` is absent from the public controller.
 
